el unwell during the flight, what should you do?","options":[{"id":"tif-q2-o1","label":"Tell the instructor promptly."},{"id":"tif-q2-o2","label":"Wait until landing so the lesson is not interrupted."},{"id":"tif-q2-o3","label":"Close your eyes and hold the controls tightly."},{"id":"tif-q2-o4","label":"Remove the headset without warning."}],"correctAnswer":"tif-q2-o1","required":true,"incorrectExplanation":"Review the lesson briefing, the current aircraft documents and the instructor-approved sequence before trying again.","successMessage":"Correct - relate the answer to the booked aircraft and the conditions on the day."},{"id":"tif-q3","type":"single_choice","prompt":"What should guide your first pitch and roll changes?","options":[{"id":"tif-q3-o1","label":"Large inputs referenced only to the instruments."},{"id":"tif-q3-o2","label":"The position of the control stick alone."},{"id":"tif-q3-o3","label":"Engine sound without an outside reference."},{"id":"tif-q3-o4","label":"Small inputs referenced to the natural horizon."}],"correctAnswer":"tif-q3-o4","required":true,"incorrectExplanation":"Review the lesson briefing, the current aircraft documents and the instructor-approved sequence before trying again.","successMessage":"Correct - relate the answer to the booked aircraft and the conditions on the day."},{"id":"tif-q4","type":"single_choice","prompt":"Before using a P92 speed, RPM, flap setting, limitation or emergency action, which source controls?","options":[{"id":"tif-q4-o1","label":"An online forum post."},{"id":"tif-q4-o2","label":"The current Tecnam marketing page."},{"id":"tif-q4-o3","label":"The current flight manual, cockpit placard/checklist and instructor brief for the booked aircraft."},{"id":"tif-q4-o4","label":"A figure remembered from another aircraft."}],"correctAnswer":"tif-q4-o3","required":true,"incorrectExplanation":"Review the lesson briefing, the current aircraft documents and the instructor-approved sequence before trying again.","succes